  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q60-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "60",
    "prompt": "Find the range of $f(x)=\\cos^2x+\\sqrt2\\sin(2x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$[-1,2]$.\n\nRewrite $f(x)=\\frac12+\\frac12\\cos2x+\\sqrt2\\sin2x$; its oscillating part has amplitude $\\frac32$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=\\frac12(1+\\cos2x)+\\sqrt2\\sin2x\\\\f(x)&=\\frac12+\\frac12\\cos2x+\\sqrt2\\sin2x.\\end{align*}$$\nThe oscillating part has amplitude\n$$R=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2+(\\sqrt2)^2}=\\frac32.$$\nThus its extrema are\n$$\\begin{align*}f_{\\min}&=\\frac12-\\frac32=-1\\\\f_{\\max}&=\\frac12+\\frac32=2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe range is $[-1,2]$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
